ciety and  there's not a lot of that because in in  the Asian Community people want to act  like drug use doesn't exist and it's  almost like completely frowned upon and  you don't want to bring up that you have  a drug problem because I don't know if a  lot of first generation second  generation Asian parents would  understand before just kicking them out  completely or disowning them because  it's just so strict and I was blessed to  have a mom  that was not really like that but  I've watched a lot of my friends go  through homelessness and getting kicked  out of the house or leaving the house  because their the parents aren't going  to seek help for their kids or not  saying all parents are going to do that  but a lot of Asian parents are pretty  hard on them very strict you know kick  them to the curb learn your hard lessons  whatever the case is right  what would you say was your lowest point  when you were  you're using my lowest point was when I  snuck back into my mom's apartment but  she was she had already moved out and  she told me that I couldn't come back I  snuck back in and there was this  abandoned unit in the basement where  like the worker kept all of his like  work stuff  and I slept down there for a couple of  days and it was super Dusty in there so  my  I got really dirty I shaved my head I  was completely bald and  I pretty much burned all my bridges at  that point because I was stealing from  whoever it didn't matter whether if it  was friends or whether if it was people  that people I didn't know and I burned  all my bridges  and at that point I fell extra alone my  mom was not helping me out and I had no  friends and I was just trying to figure  it out and  I feel like being alone in your  addiction is probably one of the worst  things you can do because then you just  sink deeper and deeper with no one to  tell you Behavior changes so drastically  that you just become alienated from  everyone exactly exactly and I just felt  like an outcast